  "result": "Perfect! All 296 tests pass \u2713\n\n**Added mergeCustomers(customers, invoices, fromId, intoId) to src/customers.js:**\n\nMerges duplicate customers:\n- **Removes** the `fromId` customer from the customers array\n- **Updates** all invoices that belonged to `fromId` to now belong to `intoId`\n- **Returns** `ok({ customers, invoices })` with the merged result\n- **Normalizes** IDs before comparison (trim, uppercase)\n- **Immutable**: Returns new arrays, doesn't mutate inputs\n\n**Error handling:**\n- `SAME_CUSTOMER`: Returned if both IDs refer to the same customer (after normalization)\n- `CUSTOMER_NOT_FOUND`: Returned if either customer ID doesn't exist\n\n**Added SAME_CUSTOMER error to src/errors.js**\n\n**Added 16 comprehensive tests** covering:\n- Customer removal from array\n- Invoice customerId update\n- Error on identical IDs\n- Error on normalized ID match\n- Error for missing fromId/intoId\n- No mutation of inputs\n- Multiple invoices from one customer\n- Preservation of other customers' invoices\n- ID normalization with spaces/case\n- Customer data preservation\n- Correct customer count after merge\n- Empty invoices array handling\n- Various edge cases and combinations",
